Fairbanks, Alaska Low-Income Housing Application Checklist

Last Updated: July 2026

Property/Program	Application	Phone	Notes
Alaska Housing Finance Corporation (AHFC)	https://www.ahfc.us/tenants/how-to-apply-rental-assistance	(907) 456-3738	Apply for Public Housing and the Housing Choice Voucher (Section 8) program.
Interior Regional Housing Authority (IRHA)	https://irha.org/irha-applications-and-forms	(907) 452-8315	Rental assistance and affordable housing programs for eligible households.
Fairbanks Neighborhood Housing Services (FNHS)	https://www.fairbankshousing.org	(907) 451-7230	Affordable rental housing and housing assistance programs.
Chenana Apartments	Contact leasing office	(907) 479-4690	Project-Based Section 8 family housing.
Little Dipper Apartments	Contact leasing office	(907) 328-0924	Income-based affordable housing.
Parkwest Apartments	Contact leasing office	(907) 479-4918	HUD-funded low-income apartments.
Kellum Place	Contact leasing office	(907) 479-2054	Income-qualified apartments.
Weeks Field Estates	Contact leasing office	(907) 479-2054	Affordable housing; accepts some Housing Choice Vouchers.
Executive Estates Apartments	Contact leasing office	(907) 479-3655	Income-based apartments.
River Point Village	Contact leasing office	(907) 328-0595	Affordable housing community.
Amazing Grace Apartments	Contact office	(907) 328-0409	Low-income efficiency apartments with sober-living policies.
Southall Manor	Apply through AHFC	(907) 451-6426	Senior and disabled housing.
Spruce Park	Apply through AHFC	(907) 456-3738	AHFC family housing.

Application Checklist

☐ Apply through AHFC (Public Housing & Housing Choice Voucher)

☐ Submit an application to IRHA (if eligible)

☐ Contact FNHS about available rentals

☐ Call Chenana Apartments

☐ Call Little Dipper Apartments

☐ Call Parkwest Apartments

☐ Call Kellum Place

☐ Call Weeks Field Estates

☐ Call Executive Estates Apartments

☐ Call River Point Village

☐ Call Amazing Grace Apartments

☐ Ask each property:

* Is the waiting list currently open?
* What documents are required?
* How long is the estimated wait?
* Can I be placed on multiple waiting lists?

Documents to Have Ready

* Government-issued photo ID
* Social Security cards for all household members
* Birth certificates (if requested)
* Proof of income or benefits
* Bank statements (if requested)
* Current landlord information
* Rental history
* Contact information for references
